{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q417292","formula":"PbZn(VO₄)(OH)","hill":"HO5PbVZn","elements":["H","O","V","Zn","Pb"],"composition":{"H":1.0,"O":5.0,"V":1.0,"Pb":1.0,"Zn":1.0},"names":{"en":"Descloizite","ru":"Деклуазит","uk":"Деклуазит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Descloizite is a rare mineral species consisting of basic lead and zinc vanadate, (Pb, Zn)2(OH)VO4, crystallizing in the orthorhombic crystal system and isomorphous with olivenite. Appreciable gallium and germanium may also be incorporated into the crystal structure. The color is deep cherry-red to brown or black, and the crystals are transparent or translucent with a greasy lustre; the streak is orange-yellow to brown; specific gravity 5.9 to 6.2; hardness 31/2.","ru":"Деклуазит — минерал из класса ванадатов. Назван в честь французского минералога Альфреда Деклуазо (1817—1897). Относится к группе деклуазита, которая состоит из пяти минералов: Деклуазит PbZn2VO4OH Моттрамит PbCu2VO4OH Сендеклуазит PbZn2AsO4OH Пиробелонит PbMn2VO4OH Чехит PbFe2VO4OH Все минералы данной группы кристаллизуются в ромбической сингонии.","uk":"Деклуази́т (рос. деклуазит; англ. descloizite; нім."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-734495","atoms":44,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[7.578,0.0,0.0],[0.0,6.071,0.0],[0.0,0.0,9.412]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":6.576,"y":4.553,"z":7.645,"el":"V"},{"x":2.787,"y":4.553,"z":6.474,"el":"V"},{"x":1.002,"y":1.518,"z":1.767,"el":"V"},{"x":4.791,"y":1.518,"z":2.939,"el":"V"},{"x":3.789,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Zn"},{"x":3.789,"y":0.0,"z":9.412,"el":"Zn"},{"x":3.789,"y":6.071,"z":0.0,"el":"Zn"},{"x":3.789,"y":6.071,"z":9.412,"el":"Zn"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.036,"z":4.706,"el":"Zn"},{"x":7.578,"y":3.036,"z":4.706,"el":"